  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "id": "mechanism_1",
      "name": "hetero-deformation induced (HDI) hardening",
      "category": "strain hardening",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "as-cast",
      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "4",
          "section": "3. Results and discussion",
          "quote": "strain gradients will exist in the soft FCC (L1 2) phase near lamellar interfaces and geometrically necessary dislocations (GNDs) will generate near the interfaces (highlighted by arrow in Fig. 4 (c)), which will induce hetero-deformation induced (HDI) hardening [39,40].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 4(c)",
          "chunk_id": "ceb87894cfe08e99:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_2",
      "name": "precipitation strengthening",
      "category": "strengthening",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "as-cast",
      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "5",
          "section": "3. Results and discussion",
          "quote": "Dislocations are pinned by Cr-rich precipitations in the BCC (B2) phases (Fig. 4(f)), indicating the precipitation strengthening effect of in-situ precipitated Cr-rich precipitations [ 2,4,5].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 4(f)",
          "chunk_id": "ceb87894cfe08e99:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_3",
      "name": "slip transmission across Kurdjumov-Sachs interface",
      "category": "deformation mechanism",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "as-cast",
      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "5",
          "section": "3. Results and discussion",
          "quote": "The co-deformation behavior of the alloy relies on the slip transmission between two phases and the special semi-coherent interface (K eSO R ) plays an important role in favoring the slip transmission [25,28,31].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "ceb87894cfe08e99:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": "6",
          "section": "3. Results and discussion",
          "quote": "Therefore, it can be inferred that the high ductility of the as-cast AlCrFe 1.5Ni2.6 alloy also originates from the slip continuity across the KS interface.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "ceb87894cfe08e99:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_4",
